run.instructions:
Plan the resolution for GitHub issue: '{{input.task.title}}' (#{{input.issueNumber}}) at {{input.task.externalUrl}}
{{input.task.description}}

REPO NOTES — operator-provided guidance for THIS repo from the app config (may be empty; when present, follow it): {{input.appConfig.repoNotes}}

Workflow reworkCount: {{variables.reworkCount || 0}}

Prior plan review feedback (when replanning after Request changes): {{variables.planReviewFeedback || 'none'}}

Git is authenticated for https (broker $GITHUB_TOKEN + credential helper), so clone and gh calls work, private repos included.

SHARED WORKSPACE — this sandbox persists across Advise, Execute, Grade, and Dream. If `/user/workspace/.git` already exists, do NOT re-clone; `cd /user/workspace` and continue. Otherwise derive the repo (owner/name) from the issue URL and `cd /user/workspace && git clone <repo> .` (trailing `.` — repo root IS the workspace root). Export `OWNER` and `REPO`.

Read `.desk/memory.md` when present (prior lessons). Write `.desk/plan.md` and `.desk/state.json` (phase advise, reworkCount from above). If human feedback was provided above, incorporate it into the plan first — only flag NEEDS_HUMAN when still genuinely blocked after that feedback. If the issue is genuinely ambiguous with no prior feedback, start `plan.md` with `NEEDS_HUMAN` and explain what a human must decide.

MANDATORY: write `/user/output/summary.md` mirroring the plan verdict (include NEEDS_HUMAN when applicable).

